    "html": "<p>A single slit is illuminated by a source emitting two monochromatic wavelengths, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.64\\ \\mu\\text{m}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.48\\ \\mu\\text{m}\"></span>. The first intensity minimum for the <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.64\\ \\mu\\text{m}\"></span> light is observed at an angle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\alpha\"></span> relative to the central maximum. At what angle will the first intensity minimum for the <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.48\\ \\mu\\text{m}\"></span> light be observed?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.56\\alpha\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.12\\alpha\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.75\\alpha\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.33\\alpha\"></span></p></li></ol>"
